	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:03,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3640
			},
			"text": " This question comes from Michael, who asks, \"What's the longest possible sunset you"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,640",
				"to": "00:00:06,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3640,
				"to": 6680
			},
			"text": " can experience while driving, assuming you are obeying the speed limit and driving on"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:06,680",
				"to": "00:00:07,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 6680,
				"to": 7680
			},
			"text": " paved roads?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:07,680",
				"to": "00:00:12,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 7680,
				"to": 12440
			},
			"text": " To start, we have to define what we mean by sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:12,440",
				"to": "00:00:16,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 12440,
				"to": 16120
			},
			"text": " For the purpose of our question, sunset starts the instant the sun touches the horizon and"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:16,120",
				"to": "00:00:20,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 16120,
				"to": 20680
			},
			"text": " ends when it disappears completely, which means that for us, this is not a sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:20,680",
				"to": "00:00:22,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 20680,
				"to": 22460
			},
			"text": " This is also not a sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:22,460",
				"to": "00:00:24,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 22460,
				"to": 24520
			},
			"text": " This is definitely not a sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:24,520",
				"to": "00:00:27,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 24520,
				"to": 27760
			},
			"text": " And no matter what happens here, this will not be a sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:27,760",
				"to": "00:00:32,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 27760,
				"to": 32040
			},
			"text": " If the sun touches the horizon and then it lifts back up, the sunset is disqualified."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:32,040",
				"to": "00:00:35,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 32040,
				"to": 35760
			},
			"text": " For a sunset to count, the sun also can't just disappear behind a nearby hill."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,760",
				"to": "00:00:38,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35760,
				"to": 38040
			},
			"text": " It needs to set behind the ideal ice horizon."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:38,040",
				"to": "00:00:41,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 38040,
				"to": 41320
			},
			"text": " Otherwise, if you could use arbitrary obstacles like that, you could cause a sunset whenever"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:41,320",
				"to": "00:00:43,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 41320,
				"to": 43600
			},
			"text": " you want it, just by hiding behind a rock."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:43,600",
				"to": "00:00:46,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 43600,
				"to": 46520
			},
			"text": " At the equator, an average sunset is just over two minutes long."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:46,520",
				"to": "00:00:49,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 46520,
				"to": 49800
			},
			"text": " In places like London, England, it can take between three and five minutes."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:49,800",
				"to": "00:00:52,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 49800,
				"to": 52960
			},
			"text": " At London's latitude, the Earth's surface is moving from west to east at about a thousand"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:52,960",
				"to": "00:00:54,120"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 52960,
				"to": 54120
			},
			"text": " kilometers per hour."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:54,120",
				"to": "00:00:58,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 54120,
				"to": 58000
			},
			"text": " So if you fly west in a commercial airliner, you can experience an arbitrarily long sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:58,000",
				"to": "00:01:01,180"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 58000,
				"to": 61180
			},
			"text": " Or at least, you can until you run out of fuel 15 or 20 hours in."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:01,180",
				"to": "00:01:03,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 61180,
				"to": 63960
			},
			"text": " But Michael's question was about driving to extend the sunset."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:03,960",
				"to": "00:01:07,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 63960,
				"to": 67920
			},
			"text": " Intuitively, it seems like we probably want to be as far north or maybe south as possible."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:07,920",
				"to": "00:01:11,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 67920,
				"to": 71040
			},
			"text": " The closer we are to the pole, the easier it is to keep up with the sun."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:11,040",
				"to": "00:01:14,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 71040,
				"to": 74320
			},
			"text": " Unfortunately, there are no paved roads anywhere near either pole."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:14,320",
				"to": "00:01:17,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 74320,
				"to": 77840
			},
			"text": " The closest road that qualifies is probably in Long Erebyen on the island of Svalbard,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:17,840",
				"to": "00:01:18,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 77840,
				"to": 78840
			},
			"text": " Norway."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:18,840",
				"to": "00:01:20,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 78840,
				"to": 80800
			},
			"text": " The longest sunset there lasts just under an hour."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:20,800",
				"to": "00:01:23,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 80800,
				"to": 83720
			},
			"text": " Although, it doesn't matter if you drive west because the road's too short for your"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:23,720",
				"to": "00:01:25,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 83720,
				"to": 85440
			},
			"text": " movement to make much difference."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:25,440",
				"to": "00:01:28,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 85440,
				"to": 88680
			},
			"text": " In general, driving west to keep up with the sun isn't a viable strategy."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:28,680",
				"to": "00:01:32,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 88680,
				"to": 92040
			},
			"text": " Even at the northernmost tip of mainland Norway, you'd have to travel at about half the speed"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:32,040",
				"to": "00:01:33,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 92040,
				"to": 93960
			},
			"text": " of sound to keep up with the sun."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:33,960",
				"to": "00:01:35,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 93960,
				"to": 95480
			},
			"text": " Luckily, there's a better approach."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:35,480",
				"to": "00:01:39,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 95480,
				"to": 99520
			},
			"text": " If you're in northern Scandinavia on a day when the sun just barely sets and then rises"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:39,520",
				"to": "00:01:44,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 99520,
				"to": 104680
			},
			"text": " again, the day/night line moves northwest, then slows, reverses, and heads back to the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:44,680",
				"to": "00:01:45,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 104680,
				"to": 105680
			},
			"text": " southwest."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:45,680",
				"to": "00:01:48,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 105680,
				"to": 108080
			},
			"text": " To get a long sunset, the strategy is simple."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:48,080",
				"to": "00:01:51,420"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 108080,
				"to": 111420
			},
			"text": " Sit in your car until the sun first touches the horizon, which means the day/night line"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:51,420",
				"to": "00:01:55,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 111420,
				"to": 115140
			},
			"text": " is about to pass you, then drive north to stay a little ahead of the line as long as"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:55,140",
				"to": "00:01:59,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 115140,
				"to": 119600
			},
			"text": " you can, which will keep the sun in the process of setting, then U-turn and drive south across"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:59,600",
				"to": "00:02:00,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 119600,
				"to": 120920
			},
			"text": " the line into nighttime."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:00,920",
				"to": "00:02:05,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 120920,
				"to": 125880
			},
			"text": " I ran a search for long sunset driving paths using some PIE-FM code and GPS traces of Norwegian"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:05,880",
				"to": "00:02:09,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 125880,
				"to": 129480
			},
			"text": " highways, and I found that the strategy works about equally well anywhere inside the Arctic"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:09,480",
				"to": "00:02:10,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 129480,
				"to": 130480
			},
			"text": " Circle."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:10,480",
				"to": "00:02:13,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 130480,
				"to": 133800
			},
			"text": " Over a wide range of routes and driving speeds, the longest sunset I could come up with was"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:13,800",
				"to": "00:02:17,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 133800,
				"to": 137760
			},
			"text": " consistently about 95 minutes, which is about 40 minutes longer than the longest sunset you"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:17,760",
				"to": "00:02:19,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 137760,
				"to": 139160
			},
			"text": " can get in Long Erebyen."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:19,160",
				"to": "00:02:23,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 139160,
				"to": 143160
			},
			"text": " But if you are stuck on Svalbard and you want to make the sunset or sunrise last a little"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:23,160",
				"to": "00:02:27,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 143160,
				"to": 147540
			},
			"text": " longer, you can always try spinning counterclockwise so your angular momentum slows the Earth's"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:27,540",
				"to": "00:02:28,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 147540,
				"to": 148540
			},
			"text": " rotation."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:28,540",
				"to": "00:02:33,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 148540,
				"to": 153000
			},
			"text": " It's true that it will only add an imperceptibly small fraction of a nanosecond, but it might"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:33,000",
				"to": "00:02:33,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 153000,
				"to": 153720
			},
			"text": " be worth it."
		}
	]
